<title>INDIA: India ONGC 1st half net falls 19 pct.</title>
<headline>India ONGC 1st half net falls 19 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Sept 1996</p>
<p>		  (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	 8,278.76   vs    10,189.56</p>
<p>    Net sales	 61,634.95   vs    64,773.07</p>
<p>    Other income     3,091.74   vs     2,908.06</p>
<p>    Expenditure     35,529.36   vs    37,130.89</p>
<p>    Interest	   4,561.39   vs     5,249.29</p>
<p>    Gross Profit    24,635.94   vs    25,300.94</p>
<p>    Depreciation    14,807.18   vs    14,265.08</p>
<p>    Tax		  1,550.00   vs     8,463.00</p>
<p>NOTE: The state-run Oil and Natural Gas Commission is India's largest producer of oil and natural gas, accounting for 90 percent of total hydrocarbon production.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11-301 2024</p>
</text>
